# Normalise line endings.
#
# Fifteen files were checked in with CRLF, mixed in among LF ones, because the
# app is edited from both Linux and the Windows host that serves it over SMB.
# The cost is not theoretical: a one-character CRLF/LF difference on a file's
# last line is enough to leave the host's working tree dirty, and the host is a
# non-bare checkout with receive.denyCurrentBranch=updateInstead, so a dirty
# tree rejects the deploy push outright. It also turns a three-line edit into a
# whole-file diff, which hides the real change in review.
#
# Everything text is LF in the repository from here on. Git still checks out
# whatever the platform wants, so nothing changes for an editor on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: byte-for-byte or it is corrupt.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.apk   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
